https://github.com/dscripka/openWakeWord/tree/v0.6.0

The Swift streaming implementation follows openWakeWord v0.6.0's feature
windowing, PCM scaling, and mel transform. It uses deterministic live-audio
warmup instead of random initial embeddings. Code is Apache-2.0, see
openWakeWord-LICENSE. Google's speech_embedding backbone is Apache-2.0:
https://tfhub.dev/google/speech_embedding/1

Optional pretrained Alexa v0.1 is by openWakeWord and is distributed unchanged
from the v0.5.1 release when selected with wake-models.pretrained.json. It is
not included in the default Hey Evener model bundle. The upstream pretrained
phrase models are licensed under Creative
Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-ShareAlike 4.0 International:
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/
See openWakeWord-MODEL-LICENSE. Alexa remains a personal-use runtime preview.
The default first-party Hey Evener classifier, its modified feature assets and
training-data attribution are described in wake-word/NOTICE.md, also bundled.
